          #RemarkOnShiftedWeilAlgebra.num_note
            %h6#note Note
            %p
              Where the formula for the differential of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(b\mathbb{R}\to \mathfrak{g}_\mu)
              has the 3-cocycle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde W(b\mathbb{R}\to \mathfrak{g}_\mu)
              has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+element"} Chern-Simons element
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi cs
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cs
                    %mo −
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cs-\mu
              is precisely what shifts the curvature characteristic
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
